ws-2026-09-27-02-write-019", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a steep cliff on Hisingen, red ochre bonded with the rock still shows ships, fish, a large deer and wave-like patterns: the Tumlehed Rock Painting, the southernmost recorded in Sweden."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-019 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the painting is on a steep cliff [S4]; it is on Hisingen [S1]; the painting was made with red ochre bonded with the rock and has survived [S5]; it depicts ships, fish, a large deer and wave-like patterns [S4]; it is the southernmost recorded rock painting in Sweden [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-057 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Tumlehed Rock Painting is a prehistoric rock painting (pictograph) site on the island of Hisingen, Sweden [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumlehed_rock_painting]; The painting is on a steep cliff [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumlehed_rock_painting]; It shows ships, fish, a large deer and wave-like patterns [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumlehed_rock_painting]; It is made of red ochre bonded with the rock, which has survived to the present [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumlehed_rock_painting]; It is the southernmost recorded rock painting in Sweden [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumlehed_rock_painting]"}]'::jsonb),
